A text link picked from the object browser keeps the picked item's catalog metadata beside its address, as `data.item` (its type, size, dates and anything a site adds; not its address or the people who made it), so a frontend can draw a link from what it links to without fetching it. The mock API's search results carry `portal_type`, `mime_type`, `getObjSize` and the creators, as Plone's catalog does. @djay
